      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Downtown Red Bud, centered around the intersection of Main and Market Streets, is a Historic District which was placed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1978.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://aboutstlouis.com/local/communities/red-bud-illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Several of the historic buildings are the Red Bud \"Opera House\" built in 1860, the Ziebold Building, built in 1895 and the Red Bud City Hall, built in 1894.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://aboutstlouis.com/local/communities/red-bud-illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Preston Brickey built a log cabin near Main and Power streets in 1820, the first European settlement in what is now Red Bud.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Bud%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Red Bud was chartered as a city on February 28, 1867.",
